   "caption": "The same assistant, embedded inside the Moodle activity.",
   "context": "Deciding exactly what is indexed\n\nThe same assistant, embedded inside the Moodle activity.\n\nThe same assistant, embedded inside the Moodle activity.\n\nDeciding exactly what is indexed\n\nThe automatic link indexes what is in your Moodle course. If you would rather choose precisely what the assistant answers from, create your own course in Minerva with New Course and upload only the documents you want.\n\nThen add a second Minerva activity in Moodle and point it at that course the first time you open it. Both activities can sit in the same Moodle course; students get whichever one you send them to.\n\nIf the automatic link did not happen\n\nWithout a Daisy offering id in the Moodle course's Course ID number there is nothing to match on, so nothing gets linked. Open Minerva settings from the course's More menu, pick the Minerva course and choose Link Minerva course.",
